interoperability information; (b) extract, copy, or reproduce the non-literal structure,
sequence, and organization (SSO) of the Agent Orchestration Architecture; (c) translate, port,
or convert the Agent Orchestration Architecture (including any of its heuristics, pacing
parameters, error taxonomy, or guard logic) into any other programming language, framework, or
platform; (d) circumvent, disable, or bypass any technical protection measure in the Software,
including but not limited to the Keychain-encrypted credential store, the local service
authentication token, the hardened local-file access guard, or any license or integrity
mechanism, or develop, distribute, or use any tool designed to do so; or (e) use access to the
Software to create, develop, or assist in the creation of any product or service that
implements, incorporates, or is derived from the Agent Orchestration Architecture. For the
avoidation of doubt, any Licensee who has downloaded or used the Software is bound by this
Section 4.5, and the availability of interoperability or fair-dealing exceptions under
Section 52 of the Copyright Act, 1957 shall not be available as a defence to a breach of this
Section 4.5 by such Licensee. Breach of this Section 4.5 constitutes both a material breach of
contract and, to the extent copyrightable expression or structural elements are reproduced or
adapted, copyright infringement.

4.6. **No AI / Machine Learning Model Training:** Use the Software, its outputs, its
documentation, or the Agent Orchestration Architecture to train, fine-tune, update weights of,
or distill any third-party artificial intelligence model or large language model (LLM), nor
sell datasets derived from the Software. *(Note: This restriction binds Licensees only and does
not restrict Licensor's own AI training or data processing operations.)*

4.7. **Preservation of Notices:** Remove, alter, obfuscate, or obscure any copyright,
trademark, attribution, or license notices in the Software, or bypass any technical integrity
mechanisms.

4.8. **No Unlawful Automated Access:** Use the Software to violate, induce the violation of, or
assist others in violating the terms of service of any website, platform, or service, or any
applicable law, including laws governing automated access, data collection, advertising, and
privacy. You are solely responsible for supervising the autonomous agent and for every action
it takes on third-party services on Your behalf.

4.9. **No Agent-as-a-Service:** Use the Software to provide managed, hosted, or
service-bureau execution of autonomous agent tasks to third parties as a commercial offering
