6.1. **Trade Secret Acknowledgement.** The Agent Orchestration Architecture (as defined in
Section 1.4), including but not limited to the agent execution loop, task-decomposition
heuristics, visual grounding models, session lifecycle management, step-streaming protocol,
error taxonomy, credential routing, authentication and sandboxing architecture, rate-limit
pacing logic, and file-access guard, constitute valuable trade secrets of Licensor. By using
the Software, You acknowledge that such trade secrets derive independent economic value from
not being generally known to the public or to other persons who can obtain economic value from
their disclosure or use, and that Licensor has taken reasonable measures to keep such
information secret, including but not limited to distribution in compiled form under this
License that expressly restricts reverse engineering, extraction, and competing use.

6.2. **No Trade Secret Rights Granted.** Nothing in this License grants You any right, title,
or interest in or to the trade secrets of Licensor. Your right to use the Software is a limited
privilege conditioned upon Your continued compliance with this License, and does not constitute
a disclosure or abandonment of Licensor's trade secret rights. You shall not, directly or
through any third party: (a) misappropriate, disclose, or use Licensor's trade secrets except
as expressly permitted under this License; (b) employ, engage, or collaborate with any current
or former employee, contractor, or agent of Licensor with access to such trade secrets for the
purpose of developing a Competing Use; or (c) solicit, induce, or encourage any current
employee, contractor, or agent of Licensor to disclose or misappropriate such trade secrets.

6.3. **Survival.** Licensor's trade secret rights shall survive any termination or expiration
of this License and shall be enforceable under applicable trade secret law, including the
Indian Contract Act, 1872 (Section 27), the common law of confidence, and any other applicable
statutory or equitable remedies, notwithstanding any termination of Your rights under this
License.

6.4. **Third-Party Obligations.** If You are an employer, principal, or engager of any current
or former employee, contractor, or agent of Licensor, You are expressly prohibited from
directing, encouraging, or permitting such person to use or disclose Licensor's trade secrets
in connection with Your work. Breach of this Section 6.4 shall constitute tortious interference
with Licensor's trade secret rights and shall entitle Licensor to seek injunctive relief and
damages without proof of actual loss.

