12.1. **Governing Law:** This License and any dispute, claim, or controversy arising out of or
relating to this License, its breach, termination, enforcement, or the Software (whether in
contract, tort, copyright, or statute) shall be governed by and construed in accordance with
the **laws of the Republic of India**, including the Indian Copyright Act, 1957 and the Indian
Contract Act, 1872, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.

12.2. **Dispute Resolution & Arbitration:** Any dispute, controversy, or claim arising out of or
relating to this License, including any question regarding its existence, validity, or
termination, shall be referred to and finally resolved by binding arbitration in accordance
with the **Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996** (as amended) and the rules of the
**Bengaluru International Mediation and Arbitration Centre (BIMACC)** or such other arbitral
institution as the parties may mutually agree. The arbitral tribunal shall consist of a sole
arbitrator appointed by mutual agreement of the parties within thirty (30) days of the
arbitration notice; failing such agreement, the arbitrator shall be appointed by the said
institution in accordance with its rules. The **seat and venue of arbitration shall be
Bengaluru (Bangalore), Karnataka, India**, and the proceedings shall be conducted in the
English language. The arbitral award shall be final and binding upon the parties and
enforceable in any court of competent jurisdiction. Costs of the arbitration, including the
arbitrator's fees and institutional costs, shall follow the event, meaning that the
unsuccessful party shall bear the costs of the successful party, unless the arbitral tribunal
determines otherwise in its award.

12.3. **Exclusive Court Jurisdiction & Interim Relief:** Subject to Section 12.2, the competent
commercial and civil courts located in **Bengaluru (Bangalore), Karnataka, India** shall have
**exclusive jurisdiction** over all disputes, suits, and proceedings arising out of or relating
to this License, including applications for interim or injunctive relief under Section 9 of the
Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 or under the Indian Copyright Act, 1957.

12.4. **Severability & Blue-Pencil Reformation:** If any provision of this License is held to
be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable under applicable law, such provision shall be modified
("blue-penciled") to the minimum extent necessary to render it valid and enforceable while
preserving its commercial and protective intent, and the remaining provisions shall continue in
full force and effect.

12.5. **No Waiver:** No failure or delay by Licensor in exercising any right, power, or remedy
under this License shall operate as a waiver thereof.

12.6. **Commercial Licensing:** For commercial licensing beyond the Beta Period, OEM/SDK
integration, enterprise or fleet deployment, or custom licensing inquiries, contact:
**legal@lidarium.com**

12.7. **Foreign Infringement & Platform Takedown Enforcement:** Licensor reserves the right,
but assumes no obligation, to enforce its rights against foreign or extraterritorial
